interface_notes:
SWITCH
- Environment variable TRON_GDN_STATS. Exactly "1" is on. Read once per process by tron::gdn_stats::env_enabled(). Other set values print: [warning] TRON_GDN_STATS='<v>' ignored: exactly "1" turns the GDN path stats on
- On-state info line per state: GDN path stats on (TRON_GDN_STATS=1) for model '<id>': rows for <n_workers> workers x <n_operations> operations

C++ (namespace tron::gdn_stats, header "tron/models/gdn_stats.hpp")
- Fixed interface unchanged: enum class gdn_path : uint8_t { token = 0, column_half = 1, amx_block = 2 }; N_PATHS_3; PATH_NAMES = {"token","half","amx"}; struct work_tally with the 11 fields of the brief.
- inline constexpr size_t path_ix(gdn_path) noexcept;  // array index of a path
- inline uint64_t stamp_if(bool on) noexcept;  // rdtsc when on, 0 when off
- inline constexpr size_t BLOCK_TOKENS_32 = 32; N_FORWARD_THREADS_1 = 1; uint64_t ONE_EVENT_1 = 1;
- struct header_facts { bool amx_compiled, amx_available, amx_gdn_enabled; size_t block_tokens, n_key_heads, n_value_heads, key_head_dim, value_head_dim, n_operations; };  (all default false or 0)
- struct gdn_job { size_t worker, n_workers, operation; uint64_t entry_cycles, exit_cycles; };
- model_stats(bool stats_enabled, std::string id, bool eagle, header_facts f, size_t workers);  rows = 2 classes x workers x f.n_operations
- void model_stats::begin_forward(forward_class cls) noexcept;
- void model_stats::note_gdn_job(gdn_job const& job, work_tally const& tally) noexcept;  // aborts on worker >= n_workers or operation >= n_operations
- void model_stats::end_forward(size_t n_token_jobs, size_t n_chains, uint64_t forward_wall_cycles) noexcept;
- row_sums sum_op(cls, operation), sum_worker(cls, worker), sum_class(cls); row_sums = { work_tally work; uint64_t gdn_jobs, busy_cycles, wall_cycles, wall_max_cycles, wall_count; }
- std::string render_summary(), render_totals(cls), render_forwards(cls), render_op(cls, operation), render_worker(cls, worker); void print_report(std::FILE*) const;
- struct forward_scope(model_stats&, forward_class cls, size_t n_jobs, size_t chains);
- void register_fuse_files(std::shared_ptr<model_stats> const&);
- forward_class, CLASS_NAMES, CLASS_LABELS, inc_relaxed, load_relaxed, max_relaxed, min_relaxed, UNSET_CYCLES_0 are using-declarations from tron::attn_stats.

run_gdn_operation (h/tron/models/gdn_execution.hpp:77-99): the 11 old parameters, then `gdn_stats::model_stats* stats = nullptr`.
Generated call: tron::run_gdn_operation<gdn_operations[i], gdn_kernels[0]>(..., worker, n_workers, outer_state.gdn_path_stats.get());
model::state member: std::shared_ptr<gdn_stats::model_stats> gdn_path_stats;  (null for a model without GDN operations)
Rows: worker index = worker_ix of run_gdn_operation (0 = forward thread, w = pool worker w-1). n_workers of the object = 1 + app_pool().num_workers().

For the chain path and the AMX path: the token-path accounting is at gdn_execution.hpp:165-172. A chain that leaves the token path must not add to head_tokens[token] and recurrence_cycles[token] there. Pass `stats_enabled ? &tally : nullptr` to advance() and time with gdn_stats::stamp_if(tally != nullptr). amx_gdn_enabled is set in model.hpp:1736-1741. Do not include gdn_stats.hpp from a translation unit that has AMX compile flags: it holds inline functions.

FUSE LEAVES (casual, read only, not exported)
- Prefix /model/<model id>/gdn (EAGLE draft state: /model/<model id>/gdn_eagle).
- Always: summary, decode_like_totals, decode_like_forwards, prompt_or_mixed_totals, prompt_or_mixed_forwards.
- Only when on: <class>_op_<I> (I = GDN operation id) and <class>_worker_<W>.
- Off state: summary has "on":false; totals and forwards read {}.

